# The `.scratch/` entry that stood here is GONE, and its constraint is still true — which is why it
# is recorded rather than dropped silently (#193 → #155).
#
# It said probes must live inside this package to resolve `@playwright/test` from
# `apps/fed/node_modules`; a copy elsewhere dies with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND. Still measured to be
# true: the repo root has `node_modules/` but no `@playwright/test`.
#
# What changed is that a probe is no longer a scratch class at all. Scratch is for PR bodies and
# commit messages — written once, consumed, discarded. A diagnostic worth running twice becomes a
# real spec under `e2e/`, and one worth running once is not worth a home. So the constraint no
# longer needs solving here: nothing should be written to `apps/fed/.scratch/` in the first place,
# and leaving it un-ignored makes that loud instead of silent. The previous instance reached seven
# files and ten days precisely because it was quiet.
